module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.TwoGeneratorNoetherianApproximation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.TwoGeneratorCoefficientBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Limits.DescendingMorphisms.BaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.TripleDescent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjAmple.DegreeOneCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.ProjQuasiSeparated

/-!
# The three corners of the two-generator square as limits over the Noetherian stages

Let `A` be a commutative ring and `f₁, f₂ ∈ A`, the data of [Stacks, Example 0EVH].
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/TwoGeneratorNoetherianApproximation.lean` presents `Spec A`
as the cofiltered limit of the spectra of the Noetherian stages `ℤ[i ∪ {f₁, f₂}] ⊆ A`, and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/TwoGeneratorCoefficientBaseChange.lean` identifies each of
the three corners

* the centre `Z = Spec (A/(f₁,f₂))`,
* the modification `X' = Proj (A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁))`,
* the exceptional line `E = 𝐏¹_Z`

with the base change along `Spec A ⟶ Spec A₀` of the corresponding corner over the **initial
stage** `A₀ = ℤ[f₁,f₂] ⊆ A`, which is itself Noetherian.  This file puts the two together: base
change along a fixed morphism commutes with cofiltered limits
(`AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeConeIsLimit`), so each corner over `A` is the cofiltered limit of
the corners over the stages, with affine transition morphisms and quasi-compact quasi-separated
stages — exactly the shape [Stacks, Tag 0B8W] consumes.  Applying that tag at each corner moves a
finite locally free module on it to a Noetherian stage, which is the reduction the proof of
[Stacks, Tag 0EXD] opens with.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.initialStage`, `…initialGen₁`, `…initialGen₂`: the initial stage
  `A₀ = ℤ[f₁,f₂] ⊆ A` and the two distinguished elements read in it.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.centerStageDiagram`, `…modificationStageDiagram`,
  `…exceptionalStageDiagram`: the diagrams of base changes of the three corners over `A₀` along
  the transition morphisms of the stage system, indexed by `Over (op ∅)`.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.centerStageCone`, `…modificationStageCone`, `…exceptionalStageCone`: the
  cones over them whose vertices are the three corners over `A`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.compactSpace_proj_modificationGrading`: **the modification is
  quasi-compact**, for every ring and every pair of elements: the two standard opens `D₊(T̄ᵢ)`
  cover it, because a homogeneous element of positive degree lies in the ideal generated by the
  coordinates.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isLimit_centerStageCone`,
  `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isLimit_modificationStageCone` and
  `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isLimit_exceptionalStageCone`: **each of the three corners over `A` is the
  cofiltered limit of the corners over the stages.**
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_center`,
  `…_modification` and `…_exceptional`: **[Stacks, Tag 0B8W] (1) at the three corners** — a
  finite locally free module on a corner over `A` is the pullback of a finite locally free module
  on the corresponding corner over a Noetherian stage.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_stageCone_π` and
  `…isPullback_exceptionalToModification_stageCone_π`: **the two projections of the exceptional
  line are cartesian over every stage**, which is what lets the comparison of a compatible triple
  be read at the stage level.
* `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.exists_stage_compatible_triple`: **the Noetherian reduction opening the
  proof of [Stacks, Tag 0EXD]** — a compatible triple `(ℱ, 𝒢, φ)` over `A` descends to the three
  corners over one Noetherian stage, comparison included.

## Implementation notes

The index category is `Over (op ∅)` in `(Finset A)ᵒᵖ`, the stages later than the initial one; it
is cofiltered because `(Finset A)ᵒᵖ` is.  The diagram of base changes and its limit cone are
`AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeDiagram` and `AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeConeIsLimit`: the limit of
`j ↦ Spec Aⱼ ×_{Spec A₀} Y` is `Spec A ×_{Spec A₀} Y`, because base change along `Y ⟶ Spec A₀` is
a right adjoint and `Over (op ∅)` is connected.  The corner over `A` is identified with that
fibre product by `CategoryTheory.IsPullback.isoPullback` of the corresponding cartesian square,
and the limit cone is transported along the identification by
`CategoryTheory.Limits.IsLimit.extendIso`.

**The initial stage is already Noetherian**, being `ℤ[f₁,f₂]`, so the three cartesian squares are
taken over it rather than over a stage produced by some descent.  What the stage system is for is
not the Noetherianity of the base but the descent of the *module*: the triple `(ℱ, 𝒢, φ)` need not
live over `A₀`, and [Stacks, Tag 0B8W] produces the stage it does live over.

Quasi-compactness of the modification is the one genuinely new input.  It is not formal: `Proj 𝒮`
is quasi-separated for every graded ring (`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjQuasiSeparated`) but
quasi-compact only when the irrelevant ideal is finitely generated up to radical, which here is
the statement that `T̄₀` and `T̄₁` generate it.

No `@[stacks 0EXD]` attribute appears: this is the index system of the reduction the source opens
with, not the tag.  Tag 0B8W is already registered, unconditionally, on
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso`, and the three
results below are that declaration instantiated.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EVH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EVH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EXD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EXD)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry CommRingCat HomogeneousIdeal

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlmostBlowUp

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

/-! ### Quasi-compactness of the modification -/

section QuasiCompact

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (g₁ g₂ : R) [GradedRing (modificationGrading R g₁ g₂)]

/-- **The irrelevant ideal of `R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁)` is generated by the two coordinates.**  A
homogeneous element of positive degree is the class of a homogeneous polynomial of positive
degree, and such a polynomial lies in the ideal generated by the variables. -/
theorem irrelevant_le_span_modificationX :
    (HomogeneousIdeal.irrelevant (modificationGrading R g₁ g₂)).toIdeal ≤
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun i : Fin 2 =>
        Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.X i)) := by
  rw [HomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal_irrelevant_le]
  intro d hd z hz
  obtain ⟨p, hp, rfl⟩ := AddSubgroup.mem_map.mp hz
  have hspan := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjPolyChart.mem_span_X_of_mem_homogeneousSubmodule hd
    ((Submodule.mem_toAddSubgroup _).mp hp)
  have hmap : Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) p ∈
      Ideal.map (Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂))
        (Ideal.span (Set.range (MvPolynomial.X : Fin 2 → MvPolynomial (Fin 2) R))) :=
    Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hspan
  rwa [Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp] at hmap

/-- **The modification `Proj (R[T₀,T₁]/(g₂T₀-g₁T₁))` is quasi-compact.**  It is covered by the two
standard opens of the coordinates, each of which is affine. -/
theorem compactSpace_proj_modificationGrading :
    CompactSpace (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (modificationGrading R g₁ g₂)) :=
  Stacks.ProjDegreeOneCover.compactSpace_of_iSup_basicOpen_eq_top _
    (fun i : Fin 2 => Ideal.Quotient.mk (relationIdeal R g₁ g₂) (MvPolynomial.X i))
    (fun i => AddSubgroup.mem_map_of_mem _ ((Submodule.mem_toAddSubgroup _).mpr
      ((MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule 1 _).2 (MvPolynomial.isHomogeneous_X R i))))
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.iSup_basicOpen_eq_top (modificationGrading R g₁ g₂) _
      (irrelevant_le_span_modificationX R g₁ g₂))

end QuasiCompact

/-! ### The initial stage -/

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (f₁ f₂ : A)

/-- **The initial Noetherian stage** `A₀ = ℤ[f₁,f₂] ⊆ A`: the stage of the empty index. -/
abbrev initialStage : Subring A := noetherianStage A f₁ f₂ ∅

/-- The index of the initial stage, a terminal object of the index category. -/
abbrev initialIndex : (Finset A)ᵒᵖ := Opposite.op ∅

/-- `f₁` read in the initial stage. -/
abbrev initialGen₁ : ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) := ⟨f₁, mem_noetherianStage_left A f₁ f₂ ∅⟩

/-- `f₂` read in the initial stage. -/
abbrev initialGen₂ : ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) := ⟨f₂, mem_noetherianStage_right A f₁ f₂ ∅⟩

/-- The transition morphisms of the stage system are affine, being `Spec` of ring maps. -/
instance isAffineHom_noetherianStageSpecDiagram_map {a b : (Finset A)ᵒᵖ} (g : a ⟶ b) :
    IsAffineHom ((noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂).map g) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsAffineHom (Spec.map _))

/-- The transitions of a base change of the stage system are affine. -/
private instance isAffineHom_stageBaseChangeDiagram_map
    (X : Over ((noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj (initialIndex A)))
    {a b : Over (initialIndex A)} (g : a ⟶ b) :
    IsAffineHom
      ((baseChangeDiagram (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) X).map g) :=
  isAffineHom_baseChangeDiagram_map _ _ _ g

/-- Every stage of a base change of a quasi-compact scheme is quasi-compact. -/
private instance compactSpace_stageBaseChangeDiagram_obj
    (X : Over ((noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj (initialIndex A))) [CompactSpace X.left]
    (j : Over (initialIndex A)) :
    CompactSpace
      ((baseChangeDiagram (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) X).obj j) :=
  compactSpace_baseChangeDiagram_obj _ _ _ j

/-- Every stage of a base change of a quasi-separated scheme is quasi-separated. -/
private instance quasiSeparatedSpace_stageBaseChangeDiagram_obj
    (X : Over ((noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj (initialIndex A)))
    [QuasiSeparatedSpace X.left] (j : Over (initialIndex A)) :
    QuasiSeparatedSpace
      ((baseChangeDiagram (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) X).obj j) :=
  quasiSeparatedSpace_baseChangeDiagram_obj _ _ _ j

/-! ### The centre -/

/-- The centre over the initial stage, as a scheme over the initial stage. -/
def centerStageOver : Over ((noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj (initialIndex A)) :=
  Over.mk (centerToBase ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))

/-- **The diagram of the centres over the stages**, indexed by the stages later than the initial
one. -/
abbrev centerStageDiagram : Over (initialIndex A) ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  baseChangeDiagram (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A)
    (centerStageOver A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The centre over `A` is the base change of the centre over the initial stage.** -/
theorem isPullback_centerToBase_initialStage :
    IsPullback (centerToBase A f₁ f₂)
      (Spec.map (ofHom (centerCoeffHom ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A
        (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))))
      ((noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂).π.app (initialIndex A))
      (centerStageOver A f₁ f₂).hom :=
  isPullback_centerToBase_coeff ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The cone over the centres of the stages with vertex the centre over `A`.** -/
def centerStageCone : Cone (centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) :=
  (baseChangeCone (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂)
      (initialIndex A) (centerStageOver A f₁ f₂)).extend
    (isPullback_centerToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.hom

/-- **The centre over `A` is the cofiltered limit of the centres over the stages.** -/
def isLimit_centerStageCone : IsLimit (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂) :=
  IsLimit.ofIsoLimit (baseChangeConeIsLimit (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂)
      (isLimit_noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) (centerStageOver A f₁ f₂))
    (Cone.extendIso (baseChangeCone (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂)
      (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) (centerStageOver A f₁ f₂))
      (isPullback_centerToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.symm)

/-- The centre over the initial stage is quasi-compact. -/
private instance compactSpace_centerStageOver : CompactSpace (centerStageOver A f₁ f₂).left :=
  inferInstanceAs (CompactSpace (Spec (CommRingCat.of
    (centerRing ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)))))

/-- The centre over the initial stage is quasi-separated. -/
private instance quasiSeparatedSpace_centerStageOver :
    QuasiSeparatedSpace (centerStageOver A f₁ f₂).left :=
  inferInstanceAs (QuasiSeparatedSpace (Spec (CommRingCat.of
    (centerRing ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)))))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B8W] (1) at the centre.** -/
theorem exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_center
    (E : (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hE : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E) :
    ∃ (j : Over (initialIndex A)) (Eⱼ : ((centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj j).Modules),
      SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Eⱼ ∧
        Nonempty (E ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((centerStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj Eⱼ) := by
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso
    (centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂) (isLimit_centerStageCone A f₁ f₂) E hE

/-! ### The modification -/

/-- The modification over the initial stage, as a scheme over the initial stage. -/
def modificationStageOver :
    Over ((noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj (initialIndex A)) :=
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)).modificationGraded
  Over.mk (modificationToBase ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))

/-- **The diagram of the modifications over the stages.** -/
abbrev modificationStageDiagram : Over (initialIndex A) ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  baseChangeDiagram (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A)
    (modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The modification over `A` is the base change of the modification over the initial
stage.** -/
theorem isPullback_modificationToBase_initialStage :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A f₁ f₂).modificationGraded
    IsPullback (modificationToBase A f₁ f₂)
      (modificationCoeffProjMap ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A
        (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))
      ((noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂).π.app (initialIndex A))
      (modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂).hom :=
  isPullback_modificationToBase_coeff ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The cone over the modifications of the stages with vertex the modification over `A`.** -/
def modificationStageCone : Cone (modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) :=
  (baseChangeCone (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂)
      (initialIndex A) (modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂)).extend
    (isPullback_modificationToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.hom

/-- **The modification over `A` is the cofiltered limit of the modifications over the stages.** -/
def isLimit_modificationStageCone : IsLimit (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂) :=
  IsLimit.ofIsoLimit (baseChangeConeIsLimit (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂)
      (isLimit_noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) (modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂))
    (Cone.extendIso (baseChangeCone (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂)
      (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) (modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂))
      (isPullback_modificationToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.symm)

/-- The modification over the initial stage is quasi-compact. -/
private instance compactSpace_modificationStageOver :
    CompactSpace (modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂).left :=
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)).modificationGraded
  compactSpace_proj_modificationGrading ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)

/-- The modification over the initial stage is quasi-separated. -/
private instance quasiSeparatedSpace_modificationStageOver :
    QuasiSeparatedSpace (modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂).left :=
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)).modificationGraded
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjQuasiSeparated.quasiSeparatedSpace_proj
    (modificationGrading ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
      (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B8W] (1) at the modification.** -/
theorem exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_modification
    (E : (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hE : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E) :
    ∃ (j : Over (initialIndex A))
      (Eⱼ : ((modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj j).Modules),
      SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Eⱼ ∧
        Nonempty (E ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj Eⱼ) := by
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso
    (modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂)
    (isLimit_modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂) E hE

/-! ### The exceptional line -/

/-- The exceptional line over the initial stage, as a scheme over the initial stage. -/
def exceptionalStageOver :
    Over ((noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj (initialIndex A)) :=
  Over.mk (exceptionalToCenter ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
      (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂) ≫
    centerToBase ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))

/-- **The diagram of the exceptional lines over the stages.** -/
abbrev exceptionalStageDiagram : Over (initialIndex A) ⥤ Scheme.{u} :=
  baseChangeDiagram (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A)
    (exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The exceptional line over `A` is the base change of the exceptional line over the initial
stage.** -/
theorem isPullback_exceptionalToBase_initialStage :
    IsPullback (exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂ ≫ centerToBase A f₁ f₂)
      (Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.projModelMap 1
        (centerCoeffHom ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A
          (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)))
      ((noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂).π.app (initialIndex A))
      (exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂).hom :=
  isPullback_exceptionalToBase_coeff ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The cone over the exceptional lines of the stages with vertex the exceptional line over
`A`.** -/
def exceptionalStageCone : Cone (exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) :=
  (baseChangeCone (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂)
      (initialIndex A) (exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂)).extend
    (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.hom

/-- **The exceptional line over `A` is the cofiltered limit of the exceptional lines over the
stages.** -/
def isLimit_exceptionalStageCone : IsLimit (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂) :=
  IsLimit.ofIsoLimit (baseChangeConeIsLimit (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂)
      (isLimit_noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) (exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂))
    (Cone.extendIso (baseChangeCone (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂)
      (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A) (exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂))
      (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.symm)

/-- The exceptional line over the initial stage is quasi-compact. -/
private instance compactSpace_exceptionalStageOver :
    CompactSpace (exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂).left :=
  Stacks.ProjAmple.compactSpace_proj_polyGrading
    (centerRing ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)) 1

/-- The exceptional line over the initial stage is quasi-separated. -/
private instance quasiSeparatedSpace_exceptionalStageOver :
    QuasiSeparatedSpace (exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂).left :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjQuasiSeparated.quasiSeparatedSpace_proj
    (exceptionalGrading ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
      (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B8W] (1) at the exceptional line.** -/
theorem exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_exceptional
    (E : (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hE : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} E) :
    ∃ (j : Over (initialIndex A))
      (Eⱼ : ((exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj j).Modules),
      SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Eⱼ ∧
        Nonempty (E ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj Eⱼ) := by
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso
    (exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂)
    (isLimit_exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂) E hE

/-! ### The exceptional line over the centre, over the stages -/

/-- **The projection of the exceptional line onto the centre over the initial stage**, as a
morphism of schemes over the initial stage.  Its compatibility with the two structure morphisms
is definitional, the structure morphism of the exceptional line over a stage being by
construction the composite of this projection with the structure morphism of the centre. -/
def exceptionalToCenterStageOver :
    exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂ ⟶ centerStageOver A f₁ f₂ :=
  Over.homMk (exceptionalToCenter ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)) rfl

/-- **The morphism of the diagrams of stages induced by the projection of the exceptional line
onto the centre.** -/
abbrev exceptionalToCenterStageDiagram :
    exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂ ⟶ centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂ :=
  baseChangeDiagramMap (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A)
    (exceptionalToCenterStageOver A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The projection of the exceptional line onto the centre is compatible with the two limit
cones, cartesianly**: over every stage the square formed by the two cone legs, the projection over
`A` and the projection over the stage is a pullback square.

This is the centre-side companion of
`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_exceptionalToModification_stageCone_π`, and the two together are
what let the *comparison* `φ` of a compatible triple — a morphism living on the exceptional line
over `A` between the restrictions of a module on the centre and a module on the modification — be
read as a morphism between modules pulled back from one stage, which is the shape
`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.exists_stage_map_exceptional` consumes.  Its cartesianness comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeCone_π_isPullback` transported along the two identifications of the
corners over `A` with fibre products by `AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeMap_comp_isoPullback_inv`,
whose second hypothesis here is `Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_coeff`. -/
theorem isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_stageCone_π (a : Over (initialIndex A)) :
    IsPullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app a)
      (exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂)
      ((exceptionalToCenterStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).app a)
      ((centerStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app a) :=
  (baseChangeCone_π_isPullback (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A)
    (exceptionalToCenterStageOver A f₁ f₂) (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) a).of_iso
      (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.symm (Iso.refl _)
      (isPullback_centerToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.symm (Iso.refl _)
      ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc _ _).symm)
      (baseChangeMap_comp_isoPullback_inv _ (exceptionalToCenterStageOver A f₁ f₂)
        (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂)
        (isPullback_centerToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂)
        (exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂) rfl
        (isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_coeff ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A
          (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)).w)
      ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm)
      ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc _ _).symm)

/-! ### The exceptional line inside the modification, over the stages -/

/-- **The inclusion of the exceptional line into the modification over the initial stage**, as a
morphism of schemes over the initial stage.  Its compatibility with the two structure morphisms is
the commutativity of the two-generator square over the initial stage. -/
def exceptionalToModificationStageOver :
    exceptionalStageOver A f₁ f₂ ⟶ modificationStageOver A f₁ f₂ :=
  letI := (twoGeneratorSquare ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
    (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)).modificationGraded
  Over.homMk (exceptionalToModification ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
      (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂))
    (twoGenerator_isPullback ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂)
      (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)).w

/-- **The morphism of the diagrams of stages induced by the inclusion of the exceptional line into
the modification.** -/
abbrev exceptionalToModificationStageDiagram :
    exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂ ⟶ modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂ :=
  baseChangeDiagramMap (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A)
    (exceptionalToModificationStageOver A f₁ f₂)

/-- **The inclusion of the exceptional line into the modification is compatible with the two limit
cones, cartesianly**: over every stage the square formed by the two cone legs, the inclusion over
`A` and the inclusion over the stage is a pullback square.

The commutativity of this square is the content the Noetherian reduction of [Stacks, Tag 0EXD]
needs in order to descend a morphism living over the exceptional line together with the two
modules it compares: a module on the modification over a stage restricts to a module on the
exceptional line over the same stage, and the restriction commutes with the two limit
projections.  Its cartesianness comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeCone_π_isPullback`, transported along the two identifications of the
corners over `A` with fibre products; the transport is
`AlgebraicGeometry.baseChangeMap_comp_isoPullback_inv`, whose second hypothesis at this square is
`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.exceptionalToModification_comp_modificationCoeffProjMap`. -/
theorem isPullback_exceptionalToModification_stageCone_π (a : Over (initialIndex A)) :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A f₁ f₂).modificationGraded
    IsPullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app a)
      (exceptionalToModification A f₁ f₂)
      ((exceptionalToModificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).app a)
      ((modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app a) := by
  let := (twoGeneratorSquare A f₁ f₂).modificationGraded
  refine (baseChangeCone_π_isPullback (noetherianStageSpecDiagram A f₁ f₂) (initialIndex A)
    (exceptionalToModificationStageOver A f₁ f₂) (noetherianStageSpecCone A f₁ f₂) a).of_iso
      (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.symm (Iso.refl _)
      (isPullback_modificationToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂).isoPullback.symm (Iso.refl _)
      ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc _ _).symm)
      (baseChangeMap_comp_isoPullback_inv _ (exceptionalToModificationStageOver A f₁ f₂)
        (isPullback_exceptionalToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂)
        (isPullback_modificationToBase_initialStage A f₁ f₂)
        (exceptionalToModification A f₁ f₂) (twoGenerator_isPullback A f₁ f₂).w
        (exceptionalToModification_comp_modificationCoeffProjMap
          ↥(initialStage A f₁ f₂) A (initialGen₁ A f₁ f₂) (initialGen₂ A f₁ f₂)))
      ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Category.id_comp _).symm)
      ((Category.comp_id _).trans (Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc _ _).symm)

/-! ### A single stage for all three corners -/

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0B8W] (1) at the three corners simultaneously, over one common stage.**  Given
a finite locally free module on each of the centre, the modification and the exceptional line over
`A`, there is a *single* Noetherian stage `j` and a finite locally free module on each of the three
corners over `j` pulling back to the three given ones.

`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_center`,
`…_modification` and `…_exceptional` each produce their own stage, and nothing in those statements
merges them; but the three diagrams are indexed by one and the same category
`Over (initialIndex A)`, which is cofiltered (`CategoryTheory.IsCofiltered.over`, the index
category being
`(Finset A)ᵒᵖ` with `initialIndex A` terminal).  So a stage below all three exists, and the three
modules are carried to it by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_of_hom`.

This is the form the Noetherian reduction of [Stacks, Tag 0EXD] consumes: a compatible triple over
`A` is a triple of modules *together with* comparisons over the exceptional line, and those
comparisons can only be descended once all three modules live over one stage. -/
theorem exists_common_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso
    (Ec : (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hEc : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Ec)
    (Em : (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hEm : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Em)
    (Ee : (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hEe : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Ee) :
    ∃ (j : Over (initialIndex A))
      (Ecj : ((centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj j).Modules)
      (Emj : ((modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj j).Modules)
      (Eej : ((exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj j).Modules),
      SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Ecj ∧
        SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Emj ∧
        SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Eej ∧
        Nonempty (Ec ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((centerStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj Ecj) ∧
        Nonempty (Em ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj Emj) ∧
        Nonempty (Ee ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj Eej) := by
  obtain ⟨jc, Ecj, hEcj, ⟨ec⟩⟩ :=
    exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_center A f₁ f₂ Ec hEc
  obtain ⟨jm, Emj, hEmj, ⟨em⟩⟩ :=
    exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_modification A f₁ f₂ Em hEm
  obtain ⟨je, Eej, hEej, ⟨ee⟩⟩ :=
    exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_exceptional A f₁ f₂ Ee hEe
  -- A stage below all three, by cofilteredness of the index category.
  obtain ⟨Ecj', hEcj', hc⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_of_hom
      (centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂)
      (IsCofiltered.minToLeft (IsCofiltered.min jc jm) je ≫ IsCofiltered.minToLeft jc jm)
      Ecj hEcj ec
  obtain ⟨Emj', hEmj', hm⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_of_hom
      (modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂)
      (IsCofiltered.minToLeft (IsCofiltered.min jc jm) je ≫ IsCofiltered.minToRight jc jm)
      Emj hEmj em
  obtain ⟨Eej', hEej', he⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_of_hom
      (exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂)
      (IsCofiltered.minToRight (IsCofiltered.min jc jm) je) Eej hEej ee
  exact ⟨IsCofiltered.min (IsCofiltered.min jc jm) je, Ecj', Emj', Eej',
    hEcj', hEmj', hEej', hc, hm, he⟩

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 01ZR] (2) at the exceptional line: a morphism between modules pulled back from
a stage descends to a stage.**  Given finite locally free modules `F`, `G` on the exceptional line
over a stage `j` and a morphism between their pullbacks to the exceptional line over `A`, the
morphism is itself pulled back from a morphism over some stage `k` mapping to `j`.

This is the second half of the Noetherian reduction of [Stacks, Tag 0EXD]: after
`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.exists_common_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso` has put the three
modules of a compatible triple over one stage, the *comparison* over the exceptional line — the
datum `φ` which makes the triple an object of the categorical fibre product — must be descended
too, and it descends only after a further shrinking of the stage.  The modules are of finite
presentation because they are finite locally free, which is the hypothesis
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_map_of_pullback_canonical_of_isLimit'` asks for; the
quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of the stages are the same instances that
`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.exists_stage_isFiniteLocallyFree_pullback_iso_exceptional` uses. -/
theorem exists_stage_map_exceptional (j : Over (initialIndex A))
    (F G : ((exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj j).Modules)
    (hF : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} F)
    (hG : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} G)
    (φ : (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj F ⟶
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)).obj G) :
    ∃ (k : Over (initialIndex A)) (ε : k ⟶ j)
      (φk : (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).map ε)).obj F ⟶
        (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).map ε)).obj G),
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app k)).map φk ≫
          Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.canHom
            ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app k)
            ((exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).map ε)
            ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)
            ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).w ε) G =
        Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.canHom
            ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app k)
            ((exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).map ε)
            ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app j)
            ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).w ε) F ≫ φ := by
  have : F.IsFinitePresentation :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.isFinitePresentation F hF
  have : G.IsFinitePresentation :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.isFinitePresentation G hG
  exact Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_map_of_pullback_canonical_of_isLimit'
    (exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂)
    (isLimit_exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂) j F G φ

/-! ### The Noetherian reduction at a compatible triple -/

section Triple

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits

/-- **The Noetherian reduction opening the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0EXD], at the two-generator
square of [Stacks, Example 0EVH].**

A *compatible triple* over `A` is a finite locally free module `Ec` on the centre
`Z = Spec (A/(f₁,f₂))`, a finite locally free module `Em` on the modification
`X' = Proj (A[T₀,T₁]/(f₂T₀-f₁T₁))`, and an isomorphism `φ : Ec|_E ≅ Em|_E` over the exceptional
line `E = 𝐏¹_Z`.  Then the whole triple descends to the three corners over **one** Noetherian
stage `k`: there are finite locally free modules `Eck` on the centre over `k` and `Emk` on the
modification over `k`, pulling back to `Ec` and `Em`, and an isomorphism `φk` of their
restrictions to the exceptional line over `k` whose pullback to the exceptional line over `A` is
`φ`.

The pullback of `φk` is compared with `φ` through the two descent isomorphisms and the two
cartesian stage squares
`Stacks.AlmostBlowUp.isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_stageCone_π` and
`…isPullback_exceptionalToModification_stageCone_π`; that composite is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.stageComparison`, so the conclusion is the single equation
`stageComparison … φ = (π_E k)^* φk`.

This is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_stage_compatibleTriple_single`
instantiated at the three stage systems of this file, with the two compatibilities supplied by
the two cartesian stage squares and the nine quasi-compactness, quasi-separatedness and
affineness facts supplied exactly as the three single-corner descents above supply them.  This is
the reduction the source's proof opens with — after it, the base may be assumed Noetherian, which
is what makes a finite locally free module coherent and hence [Stacks, Tag 01Y3] available. -/
theorem exists_stage_compatible_triple
    (Ec : (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hEc : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Ec)
    (Em : (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂).pt.Modules)
    (hEm : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Em)
    (φ : letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A f₁ f₂).modificationGraded
      (Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂)).obj Ec ≅
        (Scheme.Modules.pullback (exceptionalToModification A f₁ f₂)).obj Em) :
    letI := (twoGeneratorSquare A f₁ f₂).modificationGraded
    ∃ (k : Over (initialIndex A))
      (Eck : ((centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj k).Modules)
      (Emk : ((modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).obj k).Modules)
      (ιc : Ec ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((centerStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app k)).obj Eck)
      (ιm : Em ≅ (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app k)).obj Emk)
      (φk : (Scheme.Modules.pullback
            ((exceptionalToCenterStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).app k)).obj Eck ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback
            ((exceptionalToModificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂).app k)).obj Emk),
      SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Eck ∧
        SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFree.{u, u, u} Emk ∧
        (stageComparison (centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂)
            (exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂)
            (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂)
            (exceptionalToCenterStageDiagram A f₁ f₂)
            (exceptionalToModificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂)
            (exceptionalToModification A f₁ f₂)
            (fun i => (isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_stageCone_π A f₁ f₂ i).w)
            (fun i => (isPullback_exceptionalToModification_stageCone_π A f₁ f₂ i).w)
            k ιc ιm φ).hom
          = (Scheme.Modules.pullback ((exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂).π.app k)).map φk.hom := by
  let := (twoGeneratorSquare A f₁ f₂).modificationGraded
  exact exists_stage_compatibleTriple_single (centerStageDiagram A f₁ f₂)
    (modificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalStageDiagram A f₁ f₂)
    (centerStageCone A f₁ f₂) (modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂)
    (exceptionalToCenterStageDiagram A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalToModificationStageDiagram A f₁ f₂)
    (exceptionalToCenter A f₁ f₂) (exceptionalToModification A f₁ f₂)
    (fun i => (isPullback_exceptionalToCenter_stageCone_π A f₁ f₂ i).w)
    (fun i => (isPullback_exceptionalToModification_stageCone_π A f₁ f₂ i).w)
    (isLimit_centerStageCone A f₁ f₂) (isLimit_modificationStageCone A f₁ f₂)
    (isLimit_exceptionalStageCone A f₁ f₂) Ec hEc Em hEm φ

end Triple

end Stacks.AlmostBlowUp

end
